From u2b295401a3ad4073 at groups.google.com  Thu Sep  5 00:40:32 2013
From: u2b295401a3ad4073 at groups.google.com (James Meadow)
Date: Thu, 05 Sep 2013 00:40:32 +0000
Subject: Extra figure being placed when plotting phylogenetic trees using 'ape' package
Message-ID: <UV_wXIPDh3k.bboL0mM7aI4J@knitr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/knitr/c/UV_wXIPDh3k/m/bboL0mM7aI4J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I have been trying to embed phylogenetic trees, using the ape package, in a knitr Rmd document. I always end up with an empty figure placement next to the actual figure being correctly plotted. I searched but could not find any documentation for this bug. An example is below. Any help in this would be greatly appreciated.

```{r,fig.height=2,fig.width=2}
library(ape)
phy <- rtree(5)
plot(phy,no.margin=TRUE)
```

This results in this output:

 <https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-Ll9In3qyuoY/UifSZuOGJGI/AAAAAAAAC4o/_xGzCocehfA/s1600/knitr_phylo_bug.png>
Or sometimes when there is an additional figure later in the document, it will be placed in the empty spot instead?

Thanks!
James

From u5eafd1ef6d900b85 at groups.google.com  Thu Sep  5 02:50:36 2013
From: u5eafd1ef6d900b85 at groups.google.com (Michael Nelson)
Date: Thu, 05 Sep 2013 02:50:36 +0000
Subject: RE: [knitr] Extra figure being placed when plotting phylogenetic trees using 'ape' package
Message-ID: <UV_wXIPDh3k.BUKpDg-U2wEJ@knitr.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <UV_wXIPDh3k.bboL0mM7aI4J@knitr.groups.google.com>
References: <UV_wXIPDh3k.bboL0mM7aI4J@knitr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/knitr/c/UV_wXIPDh3k/m/BUKpDg-U2wEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This appears to be a result of `plot.phylo` opening two devices - perhaps due to the way it saves components of the last recorded plot.

A short term work around would be to use `fig.keep = 'last'`,

```{r,fig.height=2,fig.width=2, fig.keep= 'last'}

library(ape)
phy <- rtree(5)
plot(phy,no.margin=TRUE)
```

