On Thu, Sep 26, 2013 at 10:42 AM, Michael Friendly
<michael....@gmail.com> wrote:
> This bug is actually more general than I thought.  In my example, it was
> triggered by the \texttt{1:10}
> in fig1, and thus all fig.cap containing some Latex code are prone to this
> error in the
> composing of the fig.scap.
>
> The work-around for now is to use fig.scap='' whenever you use Latex code
> withing a fig.cap.
> The following now works:
>
>
> % !Rnw weave = knitr
> \documentclass{article}
>
> <<knitr-setup, include=FALSE>>=
> options(width=70)
> opts_chunk$set(fig.align='center', fig.height=6, fig.width=7,
> fig.pos='hbt!')
> opts_chunk$set(out.width = '.6\\linewidth')
>
> @
>
> \begin{document}
> Testing fig ref in a fig caption...
>
> Plot one figure...
>
> <<fig1, fig.cap='Plot of \\texttt{1:10}', fig.scap=''>>=
>
> plot(1:10)
> @
> Then, refer to it in another...
>
> <<fig2, fig.cap='The same plot shown in Figure \\ref{fig:fig1}',
> fig.scap=''>>=
> plot(1:10)
> @
> \end{document}

